    "created_at": "2026-09-16T22:44:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-16T22:44:30Z",
    "body": "> I assume there are use cases for styling the parent\n\n@zcorpan correct: the specific functionality I had in mind when saying \"before contents (or perhaps end tag)\" rather than \"before start tag\" was the special `:scope` selector which specifically targets the parent; for example:\n\n```html\n<div>\n  <style>@scope { :scope { background-color: red; } }</style>\n</div>\n```\n\n(I believe `&` does the same thing, though off the top of my head I'm not sure what the difference is.)\n\nSo that should be roughly equivalent to:\n```html\n<div style=\"background-color: red;\"></div>\n```",
